          "Build explicit constituent relationships with the Asian (4.19%) and Hispanic (3.88%) communities; an unopposed election left these populations without direct candidate engagement, creating latent opportunity for future challengers. Specific attention to workplace equity, professional credential recognition, and healthcare access for these communities demonstrates that representation includes everyone in the district, not just the white majority.",
