          "Engage the 5.76% demographic gap — roughly 1,000-1,500 constituents — with specific constituent service and legislative attention: the unopposed result may mask whether Native American, Hispanic, and other minority residents experience the incumbent as genuinely serving them or as an Anglo representative managing a Republican seat. Building authentic relationships with these communities before competitive pressure forces it is both good governance and electoral insurance.",
          "Ground legislative messaging in material economic concerns rather than partisan abstraction: at $63,492 income and 40.3 median age, this is a constituency evaluating on whether government is delivering concrete solutions to rising costs, service access, and economic stability — not ideological purity. An incumbent who leads with property tax solutions, rural healthcare access, and workforce development is more durable than one who defaults to partisan messaging.",
