          "Establish intellectual credibility with the college-educated plurality: at 43.6% college attainment, this constituency judges on policy substance and demonstrated expertise. Speak with command about housing policy, economic development, workforce training, and the education-to-opportunity pipeline; generic partisan positioning will not persuade this audience.",
          "Engage the Hispanic/Latino community (4.94%) with specific constituent attention and language access: while modest in raw percentage, this growing community's economic concerns around affordability, workplace protection, and healthcare access mirror the broader young-renter constituency and should receive targeted outreach, not passive inclusion.",
